---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is ai readiness guide in simple terms?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Do I need to memorize all of this?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How long does it take to implement?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What happens if I get it wrong?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Is this the same across all DNS providers?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Where can I get help if I'm stuck?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout title="AI Readiness: Is Your Domain Machine-Readable?" description="The AI readiness guide: the seven machine-verifiable signals answer engines and agents check, why they matter, and how to score yours."  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/ai-web-infrastructure/" class="hover:text-accent">AI Web Infrastructure</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">AI Readiness Guide</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">AI Readiness: Is Your Domain Machine-Readable?</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      Answer engines and agents evaluate domains on signals machines can verify without trusting
      anyone. This is the checklist they run through, and how to score well on each line.
    </p>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2>The seven signals</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5">
        <li><strong>Resolvable presence.</strong> A/AAAA records that answer consistently. Agents that cannot resolve you cannot cite you.</li>
        <li><strong>DNSSEC.</strong> A signed zone proves your answers weren't tampered with. <a href="/what-is-dnssec/">Enable it</a> through your host and registrar.</li>
        <li><strong>Email authentication.</strong> SPF, DKIM, and DMARC at enforcement read as an anti-spoofing, anti-phishing posture. Domains without it pattern-match to disposable.</li>
        <li><strong>Robots.txt intent.</strong> Whether AI crawlers are allowed, blocked, or accidentally excluded by stale wildcard rules. <a href="/ai-crawler-checker/">Check the verdicts</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>llms.txt.</strong> The content map that tells models what your site is and which pages matter. <a href="/llms-txt-generator/">Generate one</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Structured data.</strong> Schema.org markup that removes ambiguity about entities, products, and facts.</li>
        <li><strong>Transport health.</strong> HTTPS everywhere, valid certificates, fast responses: fetch budgets apply to machines too.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2>Why this stack matters</h2>
      <p>
        Search-era SEO optimized for rankings among links. Answer-era visibility is binary: a model
        either trusts your domain enough to cite it, or skips to the next source. The signals above
        are the verifiable subset of that trust, and unlike brand sentiment, you can fix all seven
        this week.
      </p>
      <h2>Score yours</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/ai-readiness-checker/">AI Readiness Checker</a> runs all seven live in one
        pass: DNS, DNSSEC, SPF, DMARC policy strength, AI crawler access, and llms.txt presence,
        scored out of 100 with per-check guidance.
      </p>
      
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is ai readiness guide in simple terms?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Do I need to memorize all of this?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does it take to implement?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What happens if I get it wrong?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is this the same across all DNS providers?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Where can I get help if I'm stuck?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover.</p></details></div>
<h2>Related</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/what-is-llms-txt/">What is llms.txt?</a></li>
        <li><a href="/ai-crawlers-list/">The AI crawler list</a></li>
        <li><a href="/how-to-allow-ai-crawlers/">Allowing AI crawlers deliberately</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
